# Project Scope

Purpose: define HOSSPI HMS frontend scope, invariants, and minimum runnable contract.

## Product

HOSSPI HMS frontend is the Flutter client for the full-stack hospital management system. It implements module workspaces, clinical and operational flows, and shared shell UI against the `hms-backend` API.

Product modules and boundaries: [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../../.cursor/app-write-up.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Build production-ready module workspaces, not a generic disconnected starter.
- Support Android, iOS, Web, Windows, macOS, and Linux where the Flutter project and host enable those targets.
- Support extra-small mobile screens through large desktop screens; smartwatch layouts are out of scope.
- Integrate with `hms-backend` through repositories, DTOs, and the cross-stack contract in [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc).
- Prefer Flutter SDK widgets, Material Design patterns, and shared `lib/shared/` abstractions before custom frameworks or extra packages.
- Avoid duplicate dependencies, folders, components, rules, and competing design systems.
- Module menus, routes, forms, actions, permissions, and visibility must match backend routes, permissions, entitlements, and APIs.

## Architecture invariants

- One architecture, one routing system (`go_router`), one state system (Riverpod), one design system, one shared component strategy.
- Riverpod is the single source of truth for UI data; mutations update provider state optimistically; WebSockets reconcile state — see [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc).
- Layer boundaries are defined in [`architecture.mdc`](./architecture.mdc); do not repeat them in feature code comments.

## Minimum runnable contract

| Area | Required baseline |
|---|---|
| Startup | `main.dart`, `bootstrap.dart`, provider scope, predictable startup flow |
| App shell | `MaterialApp.router`, `go_router`, not-found route, responsive shell |
| Desktop UI | menu bar, side navigation, collapsible navigation, readable content width |
| Theme | Material 3 light/dark/system, shared design tokens ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)) |
| State | Riverpod providers with override-ready boundaries |
| Localization | English ARB baseline, `l10n.yaml`, generated l10n |
| Components | Shared buttons, fields, dialogs, state views, layout helpers ([`components.mdc`](./components.mdc)) |
| Module workspaces | `AppWorkspace` + `AppListTable` contract ([`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc)) |
| Quality | format, analyze, tests, CI commands |

## Implementation standard

- Every feature follows [`feature_workflow.mdc`](./feature_workflow.mdc) and the standard `data/domain/presentation` structure.
- Reuse shared components from `lib/shared/` before creating feature-specific widgets.
- Contextual OPD and IPD work must follow [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](../../.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc) and [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](../../.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc).

